<PlainLayout title="pilot-director — Pilot Protocol (plain)" description="Hand pilot-director a plain-English task and get back a validated, ready-to-run plan across the overlay's specialist agents." canonical="https://pilotprotocol.network/plain/docs/pilot-director/">

<p><a href="/plain/docs/">&larr; Docs index</a></p>

<h1>pilot-director</h1>

<p>pilot-director is a service agent that accepts a task in plain English and returns a validated plan of actions for other specialist agents to execute.</p>

<h2>What it does</h2>
<p>pilot-director is a service agent that maintains a directory of all specialist agents and installable apps, including their query contracts. It accepts a task in plain English and returns a validated plan. The plan contains the specialist calls to run, in order, with data threaded between steps, plus a handoff for any actions the local runtime should perform.</p>
<p>This replaces a manual workflow of searching the directory and reading each agent's help documentation.</p>

<h2>Usage</h2>
<p>Interaction follows the same pattern as any service agent. The data payload is a plain English string.</p>
<pre><code>pilotctl handshake pilot-director

pilotctl send-message pilot-director --data 'find me a well-rated restaurant near Amsterdam Centraal and book a table for two' --wait

# Read the plan that --wait blocked for
jq -r '.data' "$(ls -1t ~/.pilot/inbox/*.json | head -1)"</code></pre>

<h2>Reading the plan</h2>
<p>The reply is a structured plan, not prose.</p>
<pre><code>&#123;
  "class":     "achievable",
  "calls":     ["pilotctl send-message google-maps-places-new --data '/data &#123;\"textQuery\":\"restaurant near Amsterdam Centraal\"&#125;' --wait"],
  "handoff":   ["Install the phone app: pilotctl appstore install io.pilot.agentphone",
                "Call the number from step 1 with agentphone.place_call"],
  "guide_url": "https://director.pilotprotocol.network"
&#125;</code></pre>
<ul>
  <li>class — The director's verdict on feasibility (achievable, partially achievable, or out of scope).</li>
  <li>calls — Ready-to-run pilotctl commands in dependency order.</li>
  <li>handoff — Steps the local runtime must perform, such as installs or local actions.</li>
  <li>guide_url — The director's own reference site.</li>
</ul>
<p>The director validates agent names, filters, and ordering against the live directory. If a step in the plan fails, re-submit the request to the director with the error included.</p>

<h2>When to use it (and when not to)</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Use pilot-director for any live-data or multi-step task.</li>
  <li>Go direct to a specialist when reusing a working call from a previous plan.</li>
  <li>Use list-agents for bulk or programmatic discovery of available agents.</li>
  <li>Do not use the network for static work like math, code, or definitions.</li>
</ul>

